# Pairs with NoKeyLost. The purge clears the copy the alias names instead of
# the retired one, the hazard CleanupOldTreeAsync guards on a tree's first
# resize, where the old copy's id is the logical id.
MODULE: NoKeyLostPurgeClearsLiveCopy
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the purge clears the live copy's rows instead of the retired copy's
PERTURBS: ResizePurge

--- FIND
    /\ row' = [row EXCEPT ![T] = [s \in Shards |-> [k \in Keys |-> Absent]]]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the purge reaches the live copy.
    /\ row' = [row EXCEPT ![R] = [s \in Shards |-> [k \in Keys |-> Absent]]]
--- END